The destination package declares a top-level name that shadows a predeclared identifier.
The generated file spells predeclared identifiers unqualified (error and nil in fallible
wiring, basic-type names in signatures) and no qualification can restore a shadowed
builtin, so the destination is rejected outright (regardless of whether this particular
plan would spell the name), matching the set-name rule’s trade in the other direction.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: plumb_gen.go
error-is: ErrDestShadowsPredeclared
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type string int

type Server struct{}

//plumb:build
func NewServer() *Server { return &Server{} }
